  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0164" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00501/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_cox">
              <opener>
                <seg hand="#print_manchester_university">
                  <lb/>DEPARTMENT OF
                  <lb/>ENGLISH LANGUAGE AND LITERATURE.
                  <lb/><orgName><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_xx">THE UNIVERSITY OF MANCHESTER</rs></orgName> 
                  <lb/><placeName><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_26">MANCHESTER</rs>,</placeName>
                  <lb/>M13 9PL
                  <lb/>
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_manchester_university">
                  <lb/>TELEPHONE: 061-273 3333
                  <lb/>&#x23AF;
                  <lb/>PROFESSOR G. L. BROOK
                  <lb/>PROFESSOR C. B. COX
                  <lb/>PROFESSOR J. D. JUMP
                  <lb/>
                </seg>
                <dateline>  
                  <date>
                    <lb/><space unit="char" quantity="32"/>29th September, l97l
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <seg>
                  <persName>
                    <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">W. H. Auden Esq.,</rs>
                  </persName>
                  <placeName>
                    <address>
                      <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_46">3062 Kirchstetten,
                      <lb/><foreign xml:lang="de">Bez.</foreign> St.Pölten,
                      <lb/>Hinterholz 6,
                      <lb/><foreign xml:lang="de">N.-Ö.</foreign>, Austria.</rs>
                    </address>
                  </placeName>
                </seg>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr. Auden</rs>,
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space unit="char" quantity="5"/>I enclose your railway ticket for the journey on
                <lb/>October 11th, a seat reservation for the 10 a.m. from
                <lb/>Euston, and your Pullman reservation for the 5 p.m.
                <lb/>from Manchester.<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>I will meet you at Manchester
                <lb/>Piccadilly, and I have arranged a lunch immediately
                <lb/>afterwards.<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>Philip Larkin, who is an old friend of
                <lb/>mine, has agreed to join us for lunch.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space unit="char" quantity="5"/>May I ask your advice on one minor problem.<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>Your
                <lb/>reading is the first at the Manchester Poetry Centre,
                <lb/>and we hope these readings will continue into the
                <lb/>future.<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>Should we take records for our University
                <lb/>archives of sound, or even a complete video-tape
                <lb/>recording?<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>We have all the facilities here, but I am
                <lb/>anxious that poets should enjoy themselves here and
                <lb/>not feel molested.<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>Would you object to a video-tape
                <lb/>recording, or do you think it would be better to
                <lb/>record voice only?<space unit="char" quantity="2"/>It would be very good of you if
                <lb/>you would let me have your opinion, and I apologise
                <lb/>for troubling you with this.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space unit="char" quantity="5"/>I look forward very much to seeing you in
                <lb/>Manchester.
              </p>
              <closer>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><space quantity="28" unit="char"/>Yours sincerely,
                </salute>
                <signed hand="#hand_blue_cox">
                  <lb/>Brian <unclear>C</unclear>ox<unclear>.</unclear>
                </signed>
                <signed>
                  <lb/><space quantity="31" unit="char"/>C. B. Cox
                </signed>
              </closer>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00502/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0164">
                <lb/>49
              </ab>
            </div>
          </div>
      </div>
    </body>
